---
import '../styles/live-runtime.css';
---

<section id="runtime" class="live-runtime-layer shell" aria-labelledby="runtime-heading" data-live-runtime>
  <div class="live-runtime-heading">
    <div>
      <span class="live-runtime-index">04 / LIVE RUNTIME</span>
      <h2 id="runtime-heading">The browser asks.<br />The process answers.</h2>
    </div>
    <p>
      Runtime state is not invented in the client. The Go process reports an explicitly public snapshot of
      itself: release identity, process lifetime and deployment context.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="live-runtime-console">
    <div class="live-runtime-request" aria-live="polite">
      <span>GET</span>
      <code>/api/runtime</code>
      <i aria-hidden="true"></i>
      <strong data-runtime-http>connecting</strong>
      <small data-runtime-latency>-- ms</small>
    </div>

    <dl class="live-runtime-grid">
      <div>
        <dt>service</dt>
        <dd data-runtime-service>portfolio-backend</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>status</dt>
        <dd class="runtime-state" data-runtime-status>connecting</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>environment</dt>
        <dd data-runtime-environment>--</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>orchestrator</dt>
        <dd data-runtime-orchestrator>--</dd>
      </div>
      <div data-inspect-detail>
        <dt>instance</dt>
        <dd data-runtime-instance>--</dd>
      </div>
      <div data-inspect-detail>
        <dt>Go runtime</dt>
        <dd data-runtime-go>--</dd>
      </div>
      <div data-inspect-detail>
        <dt>release</dt>
        <dd data-runtime-version>--</dd>
      </div>
      <div data-inspect-detail>
        <dt>revision</dt>
        <dd data-runtime-revision>--</dd>
      </div>
      <div data-inspect-detail>
        <dt>started at</dt>
        <dd data-runtime-started>--</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>uptime</dt>
        <dd data-runtime-uptime>--</dd>
      </div>
      <div data-inspect-detail>
        <dt>server time</dt>
        <dd data-runtime-time>--</dd>
      </div>
      <div data-inspect-detail>
        <dt>source</dt>
        <dd>/api/runtime</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>

  <button class="density-expand" type="button" data-view-mode-inspect>
    <span>inspect</span>
    <strong>release identity / process start / deployment boundary</strong>
    <i aria-hidden="true">↓</i>
  </button>

  <div class="live-runtime-boundaries" data-inspect-detail>
    <section>
      <span>BACKEND RESPONSIBILITY</span>
      <strong>Own runtime truth.</strong>
      <p>
        Process state, release metadata and the virtual portfolio shell come from Go because the browser cannot
        authoritatively know them by itself.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <span>PUBLIC BOUNDARY</span>
      <strong>Expose only what is intentional.</strong>
      <p>
        No raw Kubernetes API and no automatic hostname or environment dump. Deployment metadata is opt-in,
        length-limited and filtered before it becomes public.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <span>DEPLOYMENT PATH</span>
      <strong>Local today. Kubernetes later.</strong>
      <p>
        The API contract stays the same. A future deployment can inject release and workload identity through
        explicit environment variables or the Downward API without changing the frontend.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="live-runtime-principle">
    <span>DESIGN PRINCIPLE</span>
    <p>The frontend presents the system. The backend is the source of truth for the system that is actually running.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  import '../scripts/live-runtime.ts';
</script>
